From 3caac9d56d3807359917e9000e365daa6ef95de7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:37:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Update and revert on the device: the states stay on the
 device

The update and the revert of a behaviour integrated on the device copy one
state in the other on the device (`copyStatesOnDevice`). They then made
valid on the host the arrays of both states, which invalidated their copies
on the device, and set the tangent operator blocks to zero on the host
after a revert. The states were thus copied to the host at the end of each
time step and copied back to the device at its first integration: for a
polycrystal on a GPU, three arrays to the host and five to the device per
process and per time step, read by nothing on the host.

The states, and the tangent operator blocks set to zero by a revert, now
stay on the device, where the next integration reads them. As after an
integration on the device, the codes which read or write them on the host
make their copies there valid first, when they do it (accessors of the
materials, `Material::synchronizeOnHost`, integration on the host, see
`MaterialArrays`). The tangent operator blocks are set to zero once, on the
device, by the revert of MGIS. The update and the revert of a behaviour
integrated on the host, and the ones of the point-wise models, whose
arrays are read on the host by the other materials, are unchanged.

For the same polycrystal (600 grains on 4 MI300A, 20 time steps), with
the previous patch, the arrays of the materials are copied 20 times to the
GPUs (their first upload) and never to the host, against 400 and 560
times; the updates take 0.02 s against 2.43 s, the predictions 3.43 s
against 4.03 s (their integration copied the states back to the GPU), and
the computation 121.3 s against 126.2 s (means of three computations).

BatchIntegrationTest: an update or a revert of a behaviour integrated on
the device copies no array to the host; the states are then read on the
host after a synchronization (with the debug device of MFEM, a read
without synchronization stops the test; the direct write in a state after
an update of the test synchronizes it first). UniaxialTensileTest: the
values of the material are read on the host after a synchronization.
